# Expandable panels

Every expandable panel on an individual workflow returns to that workflow. The control reads `Back to {workflow name}`, using the workflow’s own name. Four Generations in Optimization is the reference: `Back to Optimization`. The same control is `Back to Typology Analysis`, `Back to Physarum Logic`, and `Back to Vertical Propagation` on those workflows.

`PresentControls` in `components/workflow-present.tsx` owns this. It reads the name from `.wf-board` and renders the button. A new panel uses `PresentControls`. It does not invent a second back control or a different label.

The control stays visible inside the frame. Panel content does not cover it or push it outside.

Pause and Restart stay in the workflow corner. An open panel does not add a second pair, and it does not move the corner pair.
